# The moment (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7): the realm's tales anyone might tell (the sky, the dead, the Wardens,
# the old roads), and voices from elsewhere: being noticed, homesick, mocked and admired. talk.accent comes to two who
# barely know each other, b not from where a is (topic.accent_of, topic.accent_town). Drafts, to tune by ear.

# ================================================================ Tales anyone tells

scene m7_lore_star_wolf
when topic=lore
a : See the Wolf in the stars? Chasing the moon, they say. | My father said every star's a wolf who died well. | They say the first wolves followed a star over the mountains. | The Hunter's belt points south. Follow it and you'll find summer.
b[young] #pup : Will I be a star? When I die?
b : He'll never catch it. | Then the sky's crowded. | I'd follow a pie over the mountains. | I'll stay put, thanks.
a@pup : Not for a long, long time.
a : Doesn't stop him. | It is, on a clear night. | You would. | Summer'll come to you.

scene m7_lore_first_snow_wish
when topic=lore
a : Catch the first snowflake and make a wish. | Never cut your claws on Restday. Bad luck. | If your ear itches, someone's speaking of you. | A spider on your coat means money coming.
b[honesty=frank] #frank : And if your purse itches, someone's picking it.
b : I wished for a warmer winter. Didn't work. | I cut them yesterday. Lucky me. | Which ear? Left's bad. | I've had spiders all year. Still poor.
a@frank : Ha. Hold on to it, then.
a : Wish smaller. | Safe for a week. | Left. | Wrong kind of spider.

scene m7_lore_the_dead
when topic=lore here.time=dusk|night
a : My grandmother said the dead walk on the longest night. | Leave a bowl out for the ones gone before. | They say you hear your name called the night before you die. | Some nights I'd swear my father's in the next room.
b[temper=nervy] #nervy : Don't. Not at night. Not here.
b[piety=devout] #devout : The Bright One keeps them. They don't need bowls.
b : Then I'll stay in. | The cats get it. | Then don't answer. | Maybe he is.
a@nervy : Sorry. I'll walk you home.
a@devout : Doesn't hurt, does it?
a : Bolt the door. | Cats are ghosts too. | I won't. | Comforting thought.

scene m7_lore_wardens
when topic=lore
a : They say the Wardens know every Quickened in the realm. | My cousin swore a Warden came to his village. Grey cloak, asked questions, left. | If a pup shows a gift, mothers keep it quiet. Wardens, see. | Nobody's ever seen a Warden's face.
b[young] #pup : What's a Warden? Do they eat pups?
b : Let them know. I've no gift but snoring. | Asked what? | Wise mothers. | Maybe they've not got one.
a@pup : Only the noisy ones.
a : Some gift. | He wouldn't say. Never said after. | Wise and quiet. | Don't say that.

scene m7_lore_old_roads
when topic=lore here.place=gate|wild|street
a : Who built the old roads, do you reckon? | There's a mile stone out there older than the town. | The old road goes straight through hills. Nobody digs like that now. | Found a coin on the road with a face nobody knows.
b[job=carter] #carter : Whoever it was, they never mended them.
b : Somebody before us. | Older than the hills, they say. | Somebody with time. | Spend it.
a@carter : Ha. True.
a : That's no answer. | Nothing's older than hills. | And shovels. | Nobody'd take it.

scene m7_lore_bright_one
when topic=lore here.place=chapel|street|home
a : My mother said the Bright One walks among us in rags, to test us. | Why "the Bright One"? Did it have a name once? | The priest says every candle's a prayer the Bright One hears. | They say the sun's the Bright One's eye.
b[job=priest] #priest : The Bright One has many names. All of them are listening.
b : I give to every beggar, just in case. | Lost it, I suppose. | That's a lot of listening. | Then it sees everything I do. Bother.
a@priest : All of them? That's a lot of names.
a : Wise. | Like my sister's. | It's got the time. | Everything.

scene m7_lore_comet
when topic=lore a.stage=old
a : I saw the comet when I was small. Tail across half the sky. | The winter the Sound froze, we walked to the boats. | There was a summer it never rained. Not once. | I remember when the old bridge went down.
b : What did it mean? | Walked on the sea? | I'd have liked that summer. | What happened?
a : Nobody knew. Everybody said. | Out and back. Never again. | You wouldn't. We ate dust. | Six carts in the river. Two wolves.
b : Gods. | Brave. | Gods. | Gods.

scene m7_lore_pups_tale
when topic=lore b.stage=young
a : Have you heard about the wolf who swallowed the moon? | Do you know why owls hoot? | Shall I tell you about the three foxes? | Ever heard of the tailless king?
b : Did he? Did he really? | Why? | Yes! No! Tell me! | Why didn't he have a tail?
a : Spat it out. Too hot. | They're asking who stole their supper. | Once there were three foxes, and one was clever. | Bit it off, out of pride. Never do that.
b : That's silly. | Who did? | The third one! | I won't.

scene m7_lore_house_names
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere|towns
a : Why's our street called the way it is? Ever wondered? | Every town's got a family it says founded it. | My grandfather claimed we're kin to a great House. | Names stick. Even wrong ones.
b : Somebody'd know. Somebody old. | Every family says it founded it. | So does everyone's grandfather. | Like my nickname.
a : They're all dead. | Can't all be right. | Mine meant it. | Which was?
b : ...Never you mind.

# ================================================================ Being from elsewhere: accents noticed

scene m7_acc_sorry_what
when topic=accent
a : Sorry? Once more? | Come again? | I didn't catch that. | You said what, now?
b[accent=broad] #broad : I said #greet#. It means hello. It's not hard.
b : I said it's #very# #cold#. | I asked the way to the well. | I said #thanks#. | I said #nonsense#. About the weather.
a@broad : Ah. Hello to you, then.
a : Oh. Aye. It is. | That way. Past the forge. | Oh. You're welcome. | Fair enough.

scene m7_acc_word_swap
when topic=accent
a : What did you call that? | You've a funny word for everything. | Say that word again. | That's not what we call it here.
b : What do you call it, then? | And you've a dull one. | No. You'll laugh. | Well, you're wrong.
a : Same as everyone. | Rude. | I won't. Much. | Probably.

scene m7_acc_admire
when topic=accent a.warmth=warm
a : I could listen to you all day. | You make "porridge" sound like a song. | That's a lovely voice. Where's it from? | Don't lose that voice. The town needs it.
b[tone=shy] #shy : Oh. Nobody's ever said. Thank you.
b : #topic.accent_town#. Where everyone talks so. | It's just porridge. | #topic.accent_town#. | I'll try.
a@shy : Well, I'm saying.
a : Lucky #topic.accent_town#. | Not when you say it. | I knew it was somewhere good. | Good.

scene m7_acc_mock
when topic=accent a.warmth=cold|reserved
a : Do they all talk like that where you're from? | Speak properly, or don't. | Sounds like a goose with a cold. | Is that a voice or a cough?
b[temper=short] #short : Say that again. Slowly. I'll wait.
b : Better than you. | I speak fine. You listen badly. | Better a goose than a gate. | Laugh away. I've heard worse.
a@short : ...No harm meant.
a : Huh. | Hm. | Rude. | I'm sure.

scene m7_acc_imitate
when topic=accent a.humour=merry
a : #greet#! Did I say it right? | Let me try. "Good day." No? | I'll learn your way of talking. Teach me. | Go on, teach me your oath.
b[humour=dry] #dry : Close. You've told me my mother's a turnip, but close.
b : Not even near. | You sound like a drunk carter. | Takes a lifetime. | #oath#. There.
a@dry : She'd forgive me.
a : Bother. | That's my best voice. | I've got a lifetime. | #oath#! Ha.

scene m7_acc_where_now
when topic=accent
a : How long have you been here? | You're a long way from #topic.accent_town#. | What brought you down from #topic.accent_town#? | Do you go back much?
b[stage=old] #old : Longer than you've been alive. And I still sound like it.
b : Long enough to lose my way back. | Not as long as it feels. | Work. It's always work. | Not as much as I'd like.
a@old : It suits you.
a : Will you stay? | It'll pass. | Good work? | Go at festival.

scene m7_acc_homesick_food
when topic=accent
a : What do you miss most? | Do you miss #topic.accent_town#? | Is the food different, back home? | What's the first thing you'd do, going home?
b[from=frosthollow] #frost : Blood sausage and snow light. You can't get either here.
b[from=coldwater] #cold : Lake trout, fresh. Everything here tastes of town.
b[from=oakhaven] #oak : Acorn bread. Don't make the face. It's lovely.
b[from=mirebridge] #fen : Smoked eel. And quiet. Fens are quiet.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : Lamb with mint, and a market where they shout properly.
b[from=southmeadow] #south : Apples off the tree. And cider. Oh, the cider.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : Rain. I miss the rain. Isn't that daft?
b : Everything. | Every day. | Different. Better. | Sleep a week.
a@frost : Blood sausage? You can keep it.
a@cold : We've trout. Sort of.
a@oak : I made the face. Sorry.
a@fen : We've no eels. Thank the gods.
a@lark : We shout here. Badly.
a@south : I'd go south for cider.
a@city : Daft, aye.
a : Poor thing. | You'll get back. | Course it is. | Lucky you.

scene m7_acc_same_trade
when topic=accent a.role=merchant
a : I trade with #topic.accent_town#. Good folk. Hard bargainers. | Your folk sold me a bad cheese once. | Talk like that at my stall and I'll give you a fair price. | #topic.accent_town# coin's as good as any.
b : We're fair. You're soft. | Not my folk. Other folk. | Fair to all, I hope. | Better, some say.
a : Ha. | All your folk. | Fair to friends. | Some say a lot.

scene m7_acc_pup_copy
when topic=accent a.stage=young
a : Why do you say it like that? | Say it again! | Are you from the far place? | My friend says you talk funny.
b : Because that's how it's said. | No. | Not that far. | Your friend talks funny.
a : Say it again! | Please! | How far? | I'll tell her.

scene m7_acc_city_voices
when topic=accent here.region=ridgemere
a : The city's full of voices. | Ridgemere eats accents. Give it five years. | The wharf alone's got every voice in the realm. | Half the Commons came from somewhere else.
b[accent=broad] #broad : It's not having mine.
b : And every one's complaining about the rain. | Mine's holding out. | And every one cursing. | The other half wishes they had.
a@broad : I believe you.
a : In seven voices. | Stubborn. | Fluently. | Ha.

scene m7_acc_town_suspicion
when topic=accent here.region=towns pair.band=strangers
a : We don't get many from #topic.accent_town#. | What's your business here? | Staying long? | New here, are you?
b[travelling=yes] #road : Passing through. Don't fret.
b : Now you've got one. | Work. Honest work. | Long as they'll have me. | New enough.
a@road : I wasn't fretting.
a : We'll see. | We'll see. | We'll see. | We'll see.

scene m7_acc_north_south
when topic=accent a.from=frosthollow|coldwater b.from=southmeadow|larkfield|oakhaven|mirebridge
a : You southerners talk like you've honey in your mouths. | All that sun's made your voice lazy. | Down south you say ten words for one. | Can you even say "snow"?
b : And you northerners talk like you're rationing words. | Sun makes us cheerful. Try it. | You say one for ten. | Snow. There. Horrible word.
a : We are. Words are dear. | No. | Good value. | Lovely word.

scene m7_acc_south_north
when topic=accent a.from=southmeadow|larkfield|oakhaven|mirebridge b.from=frosthollow|coldwater
a : You northerners clip every word. | Do they teach you to talk in the cold, up there? | Smile when you talk. It won't crack your face. | You sound like you're always about to say no.
b : Saves breath. Breath's warm. | They teach you to talk in a hurry. | It might. | We usually are.
a : Ha. | Before you freeze. | Try. | No.

scene m7_acc_fens_city
when topic=accent b.from=mirebridge here.region=ridgemere
a : Fen voice. I'd know it. | You're from the fens. Is it true you sleep with your feet up? | Mirebridge? You'll miss the eels. | Do fen folk really talk to the marsh lights?
b : Dry feet to you. And to you. | Keeps them dry. Try it. | Not the eels. The quiet. | They talk back. That's the trouble.
a : Dry feet. | I might. | Quiet's rare here. | Gods.

scene m7_acc_city_in_town
when topic=accent b.from=ridgemere here.region=towns
a : City voice. You're from Ridgemere. | Fancy talk for these parts. | Come down from the big city, have you? | Does it really rain every day up there?
b : Guilty. | City's no fancier than here. Just wetter. | Climbed down from it. All the stairs. | Every day. And twice on Restday.
a : We'll forgive you. | Wetter, though. | Good riddance to stairs. | Gods.
